    `cJSON_IsObject` checks whether a `cJSON` item is a JSON object. Use it to safely test a node before treating it as an object. It returns `false` for `NULL`, otherwise `true` only when the item’s base type is `cJSON_Object`. Its signature is:
    ```c
    
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool) cJSON_IsObject(const cJSON * const item);
    ```
18. `cJSON_CreateStringArray`
    Creates a JSON array of strings from `strings[0..count-1]`. Use with a non-NULL array and `count >= 0`. Returns NULL on invalid args or allocation failure; on any element creation failure, it deletes the whole array and returns NULL. Its signature is:
    ```c
    
