    ```
19. `cJSON_free`
    `cJSON_free` releases memory using cJSON’s current deallocator hook. Use it to free pointers allocated by cJSON or compatible allocators. It does nothing special for `NULL`; it simply calls `global_hooks.deallocate(object)`. The local `object = NULL` has no effect outside the function. Its signature is:
