Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library cjson using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `cJSON_ReplaceItemViaPointer`
​ Replaces `item` in `parent` with `replacement` using pointers, preserving list links and shifting later items right. Use only when `item` belongs to `parent`. Returns `false` on NULL args; `true` if `replacement==item`; updates `parent->child` if replacing first item.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Shifts pre-existing items to the right. */
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON_bool)
cJSON_ReplaceItemViaPointer(cJSON* const parent, cJSON* const item, cJSON* replacement);
​ ```
2. `cJSON_CreateArray`
​ Creates a new empty `cJSON` array node. Use it when building JSON arrays programmatically, then add elements with cJSON add functions. Returns a newly allocated array item, or `NULL` if allocation fails.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON *)
cJSON_CreateArray(void);
​ ```
3. `cJSON_DetachItemFromArray`
​ Detaches and returns the `which`th item from a cJSON array without deleting it. Use with a valid array and nonnegative index. If `which < 0`, it returns `NULL`; if the index is out of range, the underlying lookup yields `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON *)
cJSON_DetachItemFromArray(cJSON *array, int which);
​ ```
4. `cJSON_GetArraySize`
​ `cJSON_GetArraySize` returns the count of linked children in a cJSON array/object. Pass the array/object node; if `array == NULL`, it returns 0. It walks `child->next` and returns the number of items as `int` (may overflow for very large sizes).
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
