​ ```
5. `cJSON_AddStringToObject`
​ Adds a string-valued member to a cJSON object. Use with an existing object and key name; it creates a JSON string from `string`, inserts it, and returns the new item. On failure, it deletes the temp item and returns `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
CJSON_PUBLIC(cJSON*)
cJSON_AddStringToObject(cJSON* const object, const char* const name, const char* const string);
​ ```
6. `cJSON_SetValuestring`
​ `cJSON_SetValuestring` updates the `valuestring` of a non-reference `cJSON_String`. Use it only on valid string items with non-NULL `valuestring` and input. It returns the updated string, or `NULL` for wrong type, reference, NULL args, corruption, or overlapping unsafe copy.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* Change the valuestring of a cJSON_String object, only takes effect when type of object is cJSON_String */
CJSON_PUBLIC(char *)
cJSON_SetValuestring(cJSON *object, const char *valuestring);
​ ```

